1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,590
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,590 --> 00:00:04,920
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,060
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:08,340
I've been a butcher for
thirty years.

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,480
Standing on cold concrete
floors

6
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:11,660
behind that counter,

7
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:12,700
all day long.

8
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:13,920
I had my right knee

9
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,410
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:17,890
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:19,300
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:21,100
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:21,990
and it went away.

14
00:00:22,030 --> 00:00:23,050
This is different.

15
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:23,890
Tight.

16
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:24,490
Full.

17
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:26,280
Like a band around the
joint

18
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:27,590
that never loosens.

19
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:28,470
And for two years I've

20
00:00:28,470 --> 00:00:29,650
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:30,680
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:33,020
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:34,680
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,730 --> 00:00:35,470
At three months,

25
00:00:35,470 --> 00:00:36,630
give it six.

26
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,560
At six months,

27
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:39,220
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:39,970
At a year,

29
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:42,000
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,200
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:44,090
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,610
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,860 --> 00:00:46,960
Every session,

34
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:48,520
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,750 --> 00:00:49,890
I got stronger.

36
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:51,400
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:53,240
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:54,450
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,630 --> 00:00:56,340
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:57,330
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:58,890
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:00,640
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,850
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:03,270 --> 00:01:04,840
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:06,530
operation to go back in

46
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:07,580
and do it over.

47
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,530
I said no.

48
00:01:09,050 --> 00:01:10,510
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:11,340
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:11,340 --> 00:01:12,650
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:12,650 --> 00:01:14,920
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:15,230 --> 00:01:16,770
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:16,770 --> 00:01:18,380
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:19,700
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:21,270
couldn't stand at the
block long enough

56
00:01:21,270 --> 00:01:23,000
to break down a side of
beef,

57
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:25,160
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,190
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:27,370 --> 00:01:28,580
It woke me at night,

60
00:01:28,580 --> 00:01:30,380
and it turned ordinary
things,

61
00:01:30,380 --> 00:01:31,620
like getting in the car

62
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:33,070
or up off the couch,

63
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:34,150
into a decision.

64
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,320
Some days I had

65
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:36,560
to sit on a crate

66
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:39,110
in the back cooler between
customers.

67
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:40,440
After a long and serious

68
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:41,730
talk with my wife,

69
00:01:41,730 --> 00:01:43,340
I went back in one more
time.

70
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:44,820
That was the fourth set

71
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:46,500
of X-rays on this knee.

72
00:01:46,830 --> 00:01:48,220
And like the three before
it,

73
00:01:48,220 --> 00:01:50,710
the answer was everything
looks great.

74
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:52,990
No loosening, no
infection,

75
00:01:52,990 --> 00:01:53,970
nothing wrong.

76
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:55,610
Only this time there

77
00:01:55,610 --> 00:01:56,780
was no new number.

78
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,970
Nobody said give it
another six months.

79
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:00,650
There was nothing left to
give it.

80
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:01,860
I sat in the parking

81
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:02,870
lot for a while.

82
00:02:02,910 --> 00:02:03,920
Okay, I thought.

83
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:05,250
Then explain this.

84
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:07,490
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

85
00:02:07,490 --> 00:02:08,950
I hit my breaking point.

86
00:02:09,270 --> 00:02:11,290
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

87
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:13,340
Everyone in the house was
asleep

88
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:15,030
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

89
00:02:15,030 --> 00:02:16,240
with my leg up,

90
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,830
trying to find any angle
where

91
00:02:17,830 --> 00:02:19,000
it didn't feel like
something

92
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,110
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

93
00:02:21,350 --> 00:02:23,660
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

94
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:25,630
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

95
00:02:26,170 --> 00:02:27,150
And I just thought,

96
00:02:27,150 --> 00:02:28,790
is this really my life
now?

97
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,510
Thirty years behind that
counter,

98
00:02:30,510 --> 00:02:31,870
and this is how it ends?

99
00:02:31,980 --> 00:02:33,320
I can't live like this.

100
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:35,010
So I made myself a
promise.

101
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:35,840
I wouldn't go a day

102
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,420
without looking for an
answer.

103
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,120
And when I found one,

104
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,220
I'd share it with everyone

105
00:02:40,220 --> 00:02:41,570
going through the same
thing.

106
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:42,940
So I got my laptop

107
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,450
out and went looking.

108
00:02:44,570 --> 00:02:45,680
Not for a product.

109
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:46,850
For an explanation.

110
00:02:47,090 --> 00:02:48,640
Mayo Clinic forums,

111
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:51,060
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

112
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:52,590
doctor videos,

113
00:02:52,590 --> 00:02:54,100
medical animations.

114
00:02:54,270 --> 00:02:55,660
And that's when I found a
video

115
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:57,400
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

116
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:59,650
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

117
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:01,550
had been through exactly
this.

118
00:03:01,670 --> 00:03:03,400
But before I say anything
else,

119
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,960
I want to be straight with
you.

120
00:03:05,220 --> 00:03:07,460
You've already had
something work fast.

121
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:08,380
The ice.

122
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,140
The first week of a new
pill.

123
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,970
The good day after a
session.

124
00:03:12,010 --> 00:03:13,150
Then it wore off.

125
00:03:13,260 --> 00:03:15,520
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

126
00:03:15,850 --> 00:03:17,730
Fast relief isn't relief.

127
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:18,860
It's a preview.

128
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:20,440
So I'm not going to tell

129
00:03:20,440 --> 00:03:21,940
you this works fast.

130
00:03:22,070 --> 00:03:23,030
It doesn't.

131
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:25,010
But if you're willing to
be patient,

132
00:03:25,010 --> 00:03:25,890
and to look at what's

133
00:03:25,890 --> 00:03:27,870
going on around your new
knee

134
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:29,560
instead of inside it,
there

135
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:32,100
is a real reason it still
hurts.

136
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,020
And something you can do
about it.

137
00:03:34,170 --> 00:03:36,020
Let me explain what he
said,

138
00:03:36,020 --> 00:03:38,270
because this is what
changed

139
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:39,530
everything for me.

140
00:03:39,670 --> 00:03:41,460
He started with the
basics.

141
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,860
A knee replacement

142
00:03:42,860 --> 00:03:45,120
takes out the worn joint
surfaces

143
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:47,150
and puts in metal and
plastic.

144
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:49,190
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

145
00:03:49,190 --> 00:03:50,860
you had before the
operation.

146
00:03:51,140 --> 00:03:52,760
That part I already knew.

147
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,180
But then he explained
something

148
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,630
nobody had ever told me.

149
00:03:55,670 --> 00:03:56,510
He said,

150
00:03:56,510 --> 00:03:57,850
think about a swollen foot

151
00:03:57,850 --> 00:03:58,950
inside a shoe.

152
00:03:59,110 --> 00:04:00,590
The shoe didn't shrink.

153
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:02,890
Your foot is taking up
more room,

154
00:04:02,890 --> 00:04:04,460
so everything feels
cramped

155
00:04:04,460 --> 00:04:06,120
and tight and squeezed.

156
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:08,130
Your new knee sits in a
limited

157
00:04:08,130 --> 00:04:09,800
space with living tissue

158
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:11,230
packed all around it.

159
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:13,240
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

160
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,960
had to work through that
tissue.

161
00:04:15,190 --> 00:04:17,830
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

162
00:04:18,060 --> 00:04:19,550
At first that's normal.

163
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:21,260
But in some people that
swelling can

164
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:23,940
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

165
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:25,820
And swollen tissue takes
up more

166
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,830
room than calm tissue
does.

167
00:04:27,990 --> 00:04:29,450
So when you bend,

168
00:04:29,450 --> 00:04:31,160
that tissue gets
compressed.

169
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:32,530
When you straighten,

170
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:33,870
it gets pulled tight.

171
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:35,040
That's the band.

172
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,440
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

173
00:04:37,670 --> 00:04:38,530
And you start being

174
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:39,770
the one who says,

175
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:40,890
you go ahead.

176
00:04:40,970 --> 00:04:42,110
I'll stay here.

177
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:43,870
And that's exactly why so
much

178
00:04:43,870 --> 00:04:46,050
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

179
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:48,280
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

180
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,240
around the knee.

181
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:50,210
Worth doing,

182
00:04:50,210 --> 00:04:51,180
and I'd done it.

183
00:04:51,240 --> 00:04:52,560
It does nothing about
tissue

184
00:04:52,560 --> 00:04:53,640
taking up room.

185
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,850
A nerve block quiets

186
00:04:54,850 --> 00:04:56,390
the nerve carrying the
signal.

187
00:04:56,510 --> 00:04:58,900
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

188
00:04:59,220 --> 00:05:00,920
But when that irritated
tissue

189
00:05:00,920 --> 00:05:02,480
finally calms down,

190
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,940
it holds less fluid,

191
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,560
and it takes up less room.

192
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,410
Less room taken up means

193
00:05:07,410 --> 00:05:09,470
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

194
00:05:09,610 --> 00:05:11,300
That's what takes the
pressure off.

195
00:05:11,690 --> 00:05:13,170
After two years of this,

196
00:05:13,170 --> 00:05:14,750
it finally made sense.

197
00:05:15,070 --> 00:05:16,990
The problem was never the
new knee.

198
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:19,010
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

199
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:20,850
He calls it the squeeze.

200
00:05:20,950 --> 00:05:23,360
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

201
00:05:23,630 --> 00:05:25,090
I'd bought knee sleeves,

202
00:05:25,090 --> 00:05:27,350
compression braces,
creams,

203
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:29,140
half of Amazon really,

204
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:30,390
and all any of it gave

205
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:31,460
me was an hour.

206
00:05:31,750 --> 00:05:32,820
I even looked at going

207
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,700
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

208
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:36,810
But at $200 a session

209
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,590
with nothing covered by
insurance,

210
00:05:38,590 --> 00:05:39,870
that was a quick no.

211
00:05:39,910 --> 00:05:41,010
Then one night I went

212
00:05:41,010 --> 00:05:42,270
back to that knee
replacement

213
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:43,730
group and actually read
it.

214
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:45,300
Thousands of people,

215
00:05:45,300 --> 00:05:46,920
years out from surgery,

216
00:05:46,920 --> 00:05:49,190
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

217
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:50,530
nobody could explain.

218
00:05:50,900 --> 00:05:52,610
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

219
00:05:52,610 --> 00:05:54,350
the same thing kept coming
up.

220
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,360
This one device,

221
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,860
and people saying it was
the first

222
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,240
thing that made a
difference.

223
00:05:59,540 --> 00:06:01,700
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

224
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:03,020
alright, here it comes,

225
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:04,350
he's selling me something,

226
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:05,980
let me shut that down
right now.

227
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,640
I'm only here because I
made myself

228
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,610
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

229
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:10,540
that if I ever found

230
00:06:10,540 --> 00:06:11,670
something that helped,

231
00:06:11,670 --> 00:06:12,680
I'd say so.

232
00:06:13,260 --> 00:06:15,010
It's called the KenRelief
Red

233
00:06:15,010 --> 00:06:16,350
Light Therapy Wrap.

234
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:18,430
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

235
00:06:18,690 --> 00:06:19,780
It looked like the cheap

236
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,560
knee sleeves off Amazon

237
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,030
that did nothing for me.

238
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:25,220
But I went to their
website anyway,

239
00:06:25,220 --> 00:06:26,120
just to see what all

240
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:27,160
the fuss was about.

241
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:29,510
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

242
00:06:29,510 --> 00:06:32,090
charge $200 a session for,

243
00:06:32,090 --> 00:06:35,110
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

244
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:36,080
in a wrap you plug

245
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,360
into the wall at home.

246
00:06:37,610 --> 00:06:39,290
Two hundred and forty
lights.

247
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:41,340
Red at 660 nanometers

248
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:43,670
and near-infrared at 850,

249
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:45,930
run together for the
strongest effect.

250
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,640
Four strength levels.

251
00:06:47,680 --> 00:06:49,520
A five to thirty minute
timer.

252
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,640
Then I saw the guarantee.

253
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:53,490
Ninety days.

254
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:56,000
Results or your money
back,

255
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,600
no questions, no store
credit,

256
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:00,380
and you don't even send it
back.

257
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:03,100
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

258
00:07:03,100 --> 00:07:04,650
days to change my mind.

259
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:06,030
There wasn't much to lose,

260
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:07,000
so I ordered it.

261
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:08,970
Two of them, actually.

262
00:07:09,150 --> 00:07:11,060
Only the right knee was
replaced,

263
00:07:11,060 --> 00:07:13,260
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

264
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:14,950
and I'd done it for two
years.

265
00:07:15,190 --> 00:07:17,240
The left one was carrying
the difference.

266
00:07:17,340 --> 00:07:18,270
When it came,

267
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:20,450
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

268
00:07:20,450 --> 00:07:21,540
because I'd been let down

269
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:23,420
too many times to get
excited.

270
00:07:23,620 --> 00:07:25,100
What I felt was warmth.

271
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:27,260
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

272
00:07:27,490 --> 00:07:28,670
More like it was coming

273
00:07:28,670 --> 00:07:30,240
from inside the knee

274
00:07:30,240 --> 00:07:31,680
and spreading around it.

275
00:07:31,830 --> 00:07:32,870
And that was it.

276
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,700
That was the whole
experience.

277
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:35,740
When I took it off,

278
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:36,400
I'll be honest,

279
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,110
nothing dramatic had
happened.

280
00:07:38,330 --> 00:07:39,890
And after what that video
said,

281
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:41,750
that's exactly what I
expected.

282
00:07:42,030 --> 00:07:42,820
What was different

283
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:44,030
was that for the first

284
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:45,460
time in two years

285
00:07:45,460 --> 00:07:47,380
I'd done something for my
knee

286
00:07:47,380 --> 00:07:48,430
instead of to it.

287
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:49,890
Twenty minutes,

288
00:07:49,890 --> 00:07:51,060
in my own chair.

289
00:07:51,250 --> 00:07:52,850
No drive, no copay.

290
00:07:52,890 --> 00:07:54,340
They say twenty minutes.

291
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,750
I did thirty,

292
00:07:55,750 --> 00:07:56,810
twice a day,

293
00:07:56,810 --> 00:07:59,130
lowest setting that first
week.

294
00:07:59,510 --> 00:08:01,470
Once before I opened the
shop,

295
00:08:01,470 --> 00:08:03,240
once after I locked up.

296
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:04,730
I put it on the calendar.

297
00:08:04,770 --> 00:08:05,810
The first week,

298
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:06,600
I couldn't have told

299
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,960
you if anything was
happening.

300
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,080
I tried not to get

301
00:08:09,080 --> 00:08:10,040
my hopes up.

302
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:11,180
I'd had things help

303
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,370
for a week and then stop.

304
00:08:12,410 --> 00:08:14,280
But somewhere in the
second week

305
00:08:14,280 --> 00:08:15,380
I noticed I'd come down

306
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,120
the stairs without holding
the rail.

307
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,880
I hadn't decided to.

308
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:20,470
I just did it, then
stopped

309
00:08:20,470 --> 00:08:22,440
halfway down because I
realized.

310
00:08:22,680 --> 00:08:24,250
By the end of the fourth
week

311
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,360
I'd slept through the
night

312
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,620
four times running.

313
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:28,520
I stood at the counter and
finished

314
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:30,770
making dinner without
looking for the stool.

315
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:32,540
None of that is dramatic.

316
00:08:32,710 --> 00:08:33,670
All of it was gone

317
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:34,900
for two years.

318
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:36,670
A few weeks later my wife
asked

319
00:08:36,670 --> 00:08:37,580
if I wanted to walk

320
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:39,230
the long way around the
block.

321
00:08:39,410 --> 00:08:40,430
And for the first time

322
00:08:40,430 --> 00:08:41,280
in two years,

323
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,480
I said yes.

324
00:08:42,670 --> 00:08:44,250
I wanted to understand
why,

325
00:08:44,250 --> 00:08:45,760
so I read the whole thing.

326
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,380
It comes down to four
steps.

327
00:08:47,420 --> 00:08:48,060
One.

328
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,280
The tissue around a new
knee can

329
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:53,320
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

330
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:53,960
Two.

331
00:08:54,060 --> 00:08:56,790
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

332
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:57,760
so it takes up more

333
00:08:57,760 --> 00:08:58,980
room than it should.

334
00:08:59,220 --> 00:08:59,830
Three.

335
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:01,770
There's only so much room
in there.

336
00:09:01,810 --> 00:09:03,390
Bending compresses it.

337
00:09:03,690 --> 00:09:05,240
Straightening pulls it
tight.

338
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,070
That's the squeeze.

339
00:09:07,110 --> 00:09:07,760
Four.

340
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:09,740
Red and near-infrared
light have been

341
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:11,440
studied for calming that
inflammation,

342
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,550
so the swelling and the
pressure

343
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:13,630
can come down with it.

344
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:15,810
In a randomized trial,

345
00:09:15,810 --> 00:09:17,780
patients given light
therapy

346
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:19,420
after a knee replacement

347
00:09:19,420 --> 00:09:20,680
had less pain,

348
00:09:20,680 --> 00:09:23,370
less swelling and better
early movement

349
00:09:23,370 --> 00:09:24,550
than those who weren't.

350
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:27,180
A 2025 review said the
same,

351
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:28,290
and was clear

352
00:09:28,290 --> 00:09:30,010
the evidence is still
limited.

353
00:09:30,190 --> 00:09:32,090
I probably sound like a
broken record

354
00:09:32,090 --> 00:09:33,340
to the guys at the shop.

355
00:09:33,570 --> 00:09:35,930
But after two years of
doing everything

356
00:09:35,930 --> 00:09:37,990
I was told and getting
nowhere,

357
00:09:37,990 --> 00:09:39,400
you have no idea what it's

358
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:41,000
like to sleep through the
night,

359
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,480
say yes to the walk,

360
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,920
and get my life back.

361
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:45,350
So take it from me.

362
00:09:45,420 --> 00:09:47,050
Don't spend another year
waiting

363
00:09:47,050 --> 00:09:48,050
for it to settle.

364
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:50,200
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

365
00:09:50,350 --> 00:09:51,810
More than ten thousand
people

366
00:09:51,810 --> 00:09:53,730
with pain after a knee
replacement

367
00:09:53,730 --> 00:09:55,300
have already tried this.

368
00:09:55,360 --> 00:09:57,100
Some had it worse than I
did.

